From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hendra Manudinata <manoedinata@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 17:16:21 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 101/107] net: wireless: scsc: make AP mode work with hostapd

OpenWrt's hostapd/wifi-scripts bring an AP up differently from
Android's, and three things stopped it:
- set_qos_map failed with -EINVAL on anything but a connected station;
  hostapd sets a QoS map while bringing up the AP and gives up
  ("Failed to initialize QoS Map"). Ignore it on an AP/P2P GO.
- slsi_dynamic_interface_create() registered the netdev as the default
  station and set the AP type afterwards, but cfg80211 marks a non-4addr
  station IFF_DONT_BRIDGE at registration, so the AP could not join
  br-lan ("Failed to add interface phy0-ap0 into bridge br-lan: Not
  supported"). Set the type before registering.
- the static HT capabilities (RX-STBC123, greenfield) differed from the
  firmware's (0x016f: RX-STBC1), which replace them once the firmware
  runs. wifi-scripts built ht_capab from the static ones and hostapd
  then rejected it ("Driver does not support configured HT capability
  [RX-STBC*]"). Make the static ones equal the S610 firmware's.

Verified on the J4: hostapd AP-ENABLED on phy0-ap0 in br-lan (WPA2,
channel 1, HT20), a phone associates and gets a DHCP lease. hostapd
still logs "Failed to set beacon parameters" (change_beacon is not
implemented) without effect on the AP.
---
 drivers/net/wireless/scsc/cfg80211_ops.c | 17 +++++++++++++++--
 drivers/net/wireless/scsc/mgt.c          | 12 ++++++++----
 2 files changed, 23 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/scsc/cfg80211_ops.c b/drivers/net/wireless/scsc/cfg80211_ops.c
index d8724d790..d324ffbbe 100755
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/scsc/cfg80211_ops.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/scsc/cfg80211_ops.c
@@ -1475,6 +1475,12 @@ static int slsi_set_qos_map(struct wiphy *wiphy, struct net_device *dev, struct
 
 	SLSI_MUTEX_LOCK(ndev_vif->vif_mutex);
 
+	/* hostapd sets a QoS map while bringing up an AP and fails on an
+	 * error; the driver only maps on a station, so ignore it there.
+	 */
+	if (ndev_vif->iftype == NL80211_IFTYPE_AP || ndev_vif->iftype == NL80211_IFTYPE_P2P_GO)
+		goto exit;
+
 	if (!ndev_vif->activated) {
 		r = -EINVAL;
 		goto exit;
@@ -3239,10 +3245,17 @@ static struct ieee80211_rate       wifi_11a_rates[] = {
 
 static struct ieee80211_sta_ht_cap slsi_ht_cap = {
 	.ht_supported       = true,
+	/*
+	 * Until the firmware runs, cfg80211 reports these; slsi_start()
+	 * replaces them with the firmware's (0x016f on the J4's S610). Keep
+	 * them equal: OpenWrt builds hostapd's ht_capab from the phy before
+	 * the AP starts the firmware, and hostapd rejects a config asking for
+	 * more (RX-STBC123, GF) than the firmware's capabilities then allow.
+	 */
 	.cap                = IEEE80211_HT_CAP_SUP_WIDTH_20_40 |
 			      IEEE80211_HT_CAP_LDPC_CODING |
-			      IEEE80211_HT_CAP_RX_STBC |
-			      IEEE80211_HT_CAP_GRN_FLD |
+			      IEEE80211_HT_CAP_SM_PS |
+			      (1 << IEEE80211_HT_CAP_RX_STBC_SHIFT) |
 			      IEEE80211_HT_CAP_SGI_20 |
 			      IEEE80211_HT_CAP_SGI_40,
 	.ampdu_factor       = IEEE80211_HT_MAX_AMPDU_64K,
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/scsc/mgt.c b/drivers/net/wireless/scsc/mgt.c
index 7f4b908b3..29a1a3e6c 100755
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/scsc/mgt.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/scsc/mgt.c
@@ -767,10 +767,10 @@ struct net_device *slsi_dynamic_interface_create(struct wiphy        *wiphy,
 
 	ndev_vif = netdev_priv(dev);
 
-	err = slsi_netif_register_rtlnl_locked(sdev, dev);
-	if (err)
-		return NULL;
-
+	/* Before registering: cfg80211 marks a non-4addr station netdev
+	 * IFF_DONT_BRIDGE when it is registered, so an AP registered as the
+	 * default station type could not join a bridge (OpenWrt's br-lan).
+	 */
 	SLSI_MUTEX_LOCK(ndev_vif->vif_mutex);
 	ndev_vif->iftype = type;
 	dev->ieee80211_ptr->iftype = type;
@@ -778,6 +778,10 @@ struct net_device *slsi_dynamic_interface_create(struct wiphy        *wiphy,
 		dev->ieee80211_ptr->use_4addr = params->use_4addr;
 	SLSI_MUTEX_UNLOCK(ndev_vif->vif_mutex);
 
+	err = slsi_netif_register_rtlnl_locked(sdev, dev);
+	if (err)
+		return NULL;
+
 	return dev;
 }
 
